{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Therefore whoever kills Cain.</b> Therefore — because Cain was so thoroughly humbled." "<b>Sevenfold shall be avenged.</b> According to its plain sense: Cain shall be avenged seven vengeances from whoever kills him." "<b>Sevenfold.</b> A form of seven, as in ״והכבשה ישלם ארבעתים״ (2 Samuel 12:6), and do not wonder at the form שבעתים, for such is the way of Scripture, as in ״והוספתי ליסרה אתכם שבע על חטאתיכם״, ״כי שבע יפול צדיק וקם״, ״חצבה עמודיה שבעה״, ״מזוקק שבעתים״." "<b>And HaShem set for Cain a sign.</b> He gave him a sign and believed him, but the verse did not reveal it." "<b>So that none would strike him.</b> Because he had not yet been warned, and [bloodshed] had not yet been permitted regarding murder; nevertheless, He penalized him with exile." "<b>Whoever finds him.</b> Any who find him, like ״all widow and orphan you shall not afflict.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:00.448630311Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}